<section data-analytics-location="faq" class="section wrap faq-section" id="faq">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">GOOD QUESTIONS. STRAIGHT ANSWERS.</p><h2>Start with fit.<br /><em>Keep the scope clear.</em></h2></div>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details data-faq-id="kubernetes_fit"><summary>Do we need to be ready for Kubernetes?</summary><p>No. Planning can compare cloud services, simpler architectures, and private infrastructure against your actual needs. A recommendation to wait or choose another approach is a useful outcome.</p></details>
    <details data-faq-id="planning_independence"><summary>Does planning require an implementation project?</summary><p>No. A scoped advisory engagement ends with usable decisions, documentation, and team knowledge. You can implement later with us or with your own team.</p></details>
    <details data-faq-id="pricing_scope"><summary>How do you price the work?</summary><p>After a discovery call, we define the work, deliverables, assumptions, and acceptance criteria in a written proposal. Price depends on scope, complexity, and customer responsibilities.</p></details>
    <details data-faq-id="operator_ownership"><summary>Who operates the platform after handoff?</summary><p>Your qualified operator or IT provider owns day-to-day operations and incident response. We can scope scheduled advisory or platform care, but do not offer 24/7 on-call support.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

